      "thesis": "Five photographs made between 1952 and 2016 approach conflict through borders, religious and domestic space, smoke, ruins, and the uncertain aftermath of violence. Selected across two Magnum Photos 75 curations, they form a Museum acquisition undergoing accession processing whose coherence lies in how each image tests what documentary evidence can show and what remains unresolved.",
